LOCATION:Belvedere Room 3
DESCRIPTION:Human Development · Lecture XIV (Session 14)\nLecturer: Bruno 
 Martorano\n\nRequired / core readings:\n- Günther\, I. and Martorano\, B.
  (2023). Inequality\, social mobility and redistributive preferences. UNU-
 MERIT Working Paper No. 017. https://www.merit.unu.edu/publications/wppdf/
 2023/wp2023-017.pdf\n- Iacoella\, F.\, Justino\, P.\, & Martorano\, B. (20
 20). Roots of dissent: Trade liberalization and the rise of populism in Br
 azil. WIDER Working Paper 2020/118.\n- Iacoella\, F.\, Justino\, P.\, & Ma
 rtorano\, B. (2021). Do pandemics lead to rebellion? Policy responses to C
 OVID-19\, inequality\, and protests in the USA. WIDER Working Paper 2021/5
 7.\n- Justino\, P.\, Martorano\, B.\, & Metzger\, L. (2024). Can Preferenc
 es for Redistribution Explain the Impact of Austerity on Political Partici
 pation? Evidence from the UK. Oxford Bulletin of Economics and Statistics.
 \n\nOptional:\n- Giuliano\, P. and Spilimbergo\, A. (2024). Aggregate Shoc
 ks and the Formation of Preferences and Beliefs. NBER Working Paper No. w3
 2669.\n- Stantcheva\, S. (2024). Perceptions and preferences for redistrib
 ution. Oxford Open Economics\, 3(Supplement_1)\, i96–i100.\n- Hauser\, O
 . P.\, & Norton\, M. I. (2017). (Mis)perceptions of inequality. Current Op
 inion in Psychology\, 18\, 21–25.\n- Hirschman\, A. O.\, & Rothschild\, 
 M. (1973). The changing tolerance for income inequality in the course of e
 conomic development. Quarterly Journal of Economics\, 87(4)\, 544–566.\n
 - Hvidberg\, K. B.\, Kreiner\, C. T.\, & Stantcheva\, S. (2023). Social po
 sitions and fairness views on inequality. Review of Economic Studies\, 90(
 6)\, 3083–3118.\n- Starmans\, C.\, Sheskin\, M.\, & Bloom\, P. (2017). W
 hy people prefer unequal societies. Nature Human Behaviour\, 1(4)\, 0082.
